- ### Providing a typeface
+ ### Proporcionar un tipo de letra

- Naming a typeface does not make it available where the document is shown. A browser without the
- font falls back to another, and a PDF viewer substitutes. A provision closes that gap. It is an
- instance of `Typesettable` for the typeface *in a medium*. It says how that medium obtains the
- font, and which faces it can then set. It is declared once, as a [given]:
+ Nombrar un tipo de letra no hace que esté disponible allí donde se muestra el documento. Un
+ navegador sin la fuente recurre a otra, y un visor de PDF la sustituye. Una provisión cierra ese
+ hueco. Es una instancia de `Typesettable` para el tipo de letra *en un medio*. Dice cómo obtiene
+ ese medio la fuente, y qué estilos tipográficos puede componer después. Se declara una vez, como
+ [given]:

= font, and which faces it can then set. It is declared once, as a [given]:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= font, and which faces it can then set. It is declared once, as a [given]:
=
= ```scala fuel
- typecheck
+ typecheck

= font, and which faces it can then set. It is declared once, as a [given]:
